1
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,199
Can't sleep, huh?

2
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,039
Did something happen?

3
00:03:02,639 --> 00:03:03,639
It's nothing.

4
00:03:04,919 --> 00:03:06,879
Nothing? Then why come back to me in the dead of night?

5
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,479
Go ahead.

6
00:03:21,759 --> 00:03:22,639
Director,

7
00:03:24,439 --> 00:03:25,599
tell me,

8
00:03:26,759 --> 00:03:27,960
how do you judge

9
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,840
if someone is good or bad?

10
00:03:34,879 --> 00:03:37,680
You have to understand them completely.

11
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,319
Some people

12
00:03:39,919 --> 00:03:41,520
aren't necessarily bad.

13
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,560
It's just that

14
00:03:44,439 --> 00:03:45,840
you don't know them yet.

15
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,479
If he's willing to protect you

16
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,479
and doesn't hurt others,

17
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,879
he's probably a good person.

18
00:04:00,439 --> 00:04:01,240
I understand.

19
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,479
Go to sleep.

20
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:03,479
Okay.

21
00:04:20,759 --> 00:04:21,759
It's dangerous out there right now.

22
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:22,560
I'm the only one who can protect you.

23
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,160
Understand?

24
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,160
Do you understand?

25
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,040
Here's my number.

26
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:30,560
Call me if you're in danger.

27
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:35,639
I'm Yang Jingya.

28
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:47,040
We don't get to choose where we come from,

29
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,720
but we can choose how to live.

30
00:04:54,439 --> 00:04:55,680
I like you.

31
00:05:15,879 --> 00:05:16,639
Su Dahai.

32
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,480
Start talking.

33
00:05:19,399 --> 00:05:20,279
The legs in your truck bed...

34
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,319
What's that about?

35
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:24,680
I... I really don't know!

36
00:05:27,439 --> 00:05:29,279
They were in your truck, and you don't know?

37
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,000
Well...

38
00:05:31,319 --> 00:05:34,040
Just the usual, loading and delivering.

39
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:34,839
Go on.

40
00:06:01,519 --> 00:06:03,759
How long did you spend in the bathroom?

41
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:07,279
Just long enough to take a dump.

42
00:06:07,759 --> 00:06:09,160
Aside from using the bathroom,

43
00:06:09,519 --> 00:06:10,920
you were in the car the rest of the time.

44
00:06:11,199 --> 00:06:12,000
Is that right?

45
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,519
Uh, yeah.

46
00:06:28,639 --> 00:06:31,079
The victim's body parts found this time

47
00:06:31,079 --> 00:06:33,160
and those from the previous case

48
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,439
show essentially the same cut marks.

49
00:06:34,439 --> 00:06:35,360
Same MO.

50
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,439
What about the tool used?

51
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,160
Likely a chainsaw.

52
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,720
The only difference is,

53
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,959
this time, the killer put the body parts

54
00:06:41,959 --> 00:06:43,839
into a meat-packing truck.

55
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:45,839
It seems like a deliberate attempt to draw attention.

56
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,800
Any leads from the truck driver?

57
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,480
According to the driver's statement,

58
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,800
he delivers meat to eight designated markets daily.

59
00:06:55,199 --> 00:06:56,519
The market where the leg was found

60
00:06:56,519 --> 00:06:58,240
was his fifth stop of the day.

61
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,120
During the delivery route,

62
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,560
he stopped once to use a public restroom.

63
00:07:01,759 --> 00:07:03,240
However, we can't be completely sure

64
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,600
if that was when the killer

65
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,800
put the leg onto the truck.

66
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,000
Immediately check surveillance footage

67
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,360
from the meat plant, restroom, and market.

68
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,079
Once the truck driver finishes his statement,

69
00:07:15,079 --> 00:07:16,160
release him when it's time.

70
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:18,000
On the night of the crime, traffic police

71
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,560
received a report from a passerby,

72
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,279
saying they found

73
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:21,920
Chen Xue's car on Changhong Highway.

74
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,519
Her family was notified to take it back.

75
00:07:24,759 --> 00:07:25,800
This is a crucial lead.

76
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,480
Pan Ming, Sun Yue.

77
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,800
Go to the victim's house and tow the car back.

78
00:07:30,079 --> 00:07:30,639
Remember,

79
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,680
be mindful of the family's emotions.

80
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:33,920
Yes, sir.

81
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,680
Do you load the trucks

82
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,000
at this fixed time every day?

83
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:46,480
Yes.

84
00:07:50,839 --> 00:07:52,040
Are there any other angles?

85
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,720
This angle is the clearest.

86
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,879
The others are too far,

87
00:07:54,879 --> 00:07:55,920
and way too blurry.

88
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,680
Ma'am, is anyone on duty here at night?

89
00:08:02,519 --> 00:08:03,839
Are there security cameras around here?

90
00:08:06,199 --> 00:08:07,480
Alright, I'll let you get back to work.

91
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,639
Think about it carefully.

92
00:08:09,639 --> 00:08:11,279
During the entire unloading process,

93
00:08:11,279 --> 00:08:12,000
did you ever leave?

94
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:13,920
No.

95
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,519
Are you sure?

96
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,560
I'm sure. I really didn't.

97
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,279
Oh, right.

98
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:20,399
I have a video here.

99
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,120
Hey, buddy.

100
00:08:28,399 --> 00:08:29,360
Give me a hand.

101
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,639
Un- Unload it yourself.

102
00:08:32,639 --> 00:08:33,919
I'm in a hurry to get to my next stop.

103
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,679
Just these two outside are mine, right?

104
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:38,600
Yeah.

105
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,399
Why did you record a video?

106
00:08:42,399 --> 00:08:44,120
They used to shortchange me on the weight,

107
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,240
so after that,

108
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,679
I started filming when weighing the deliveries.

109
00:08:46,679 --> 00:08:48,000
Just wanted to keep some proof.

110
00:08:48,159 --> 00:08:48,720
Look,

111
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,720
the camera was clipped right here,

112
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:50,799
so it caught everything clearly.

113
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,519
The number you dialed is powered off.

114
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:24,639
Just paint it like this.

115
00:09:24,639 --> 00:09:25,559
Copy the one over there.

116
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:06,559
Hello?

117
00:10:08,279 --> 00:10:08,919
Hello.

118
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:12,159
Sorry, I was in class just now.

119
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:13,799
Did you need something?

120
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,159
Oh.

121
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,440
You got a new job, right?

122
00:10:18,679 --> 00:10:19,879
Yeah, that's right.

123
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:21,799
I've been pretty busy lately.

124
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:23,919
That's good.

125
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,320
Yeah.

126
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:27,519
Stay safe.

127
00:10:27,519 --> 00:10:28,960
Was there anything else?

128
00:10:33,639 --> 00:10:34,600
Oh, that's all.

129
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,600
Get back to it, then.

130
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,320
Hey there, sir.

131
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,960
Quite a haul.

132
00:11:31,559 --> 00:11:32,879
I already paid when I came in.

133
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:37,279
Don't get me wrong, I'm not here for money.

134
00:11:37,759 --> 00:11:39,679
I just wanted to ask you about something.

135
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:40,840
Go ahead.

136
00:11:45,279 --> 00:11:47,279
Could you take a look at this for me?

137
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,799
Is it used for fishing?

138
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,759
Isn't this just a homemade...

139
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:00,039
rake for catching grass carp?

140
00:12:00,039 --> 00:12:01,639
Yours isn't made properly, though.

141
00:12:01,919 --> 00:12:02,639
It's too long.

142
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:03,879
And look at the nails.

143
00:12:03,879 --> 00:12:04,919
They're too sharp.

144
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,000
It won't work well.

145
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:06,639
Here.

146
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:08,799
Take a look at mine.

147
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:11,320
Look at this.

148
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,399
See how rounded the nails are?

149
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,360
Yours won't do.

150
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:14,919
Right.

151
00:12:17,399 --> 00:12:17,919
Then...

152
00:12:20,919 --> 00:12:21,519
Hello?

153
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,600
Bro Hao, we found the driver.

154
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,279
He's a meat delivery truck driver.

155
00:12:25,279 --> 00:12:26,799
While delivering to Yongchang Market,

156
00:12:26,799 --> 00:12:27,960
he found Sister Xue's leg.

157
00:12:28,639 --> 00:12:29,120
Got it.

158
00:12:29,759 --> 00:12:31,039
Send me your location.

159
00:12:59,679 --> 00:13:00,440
Come in.

160
00:13:02,159 --> 00:13:02,759
Bro Wu.

161
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,440
Two cops are downstairs.

162
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,600
They're asking for Sister Xue's car.

163
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,519
I'll find a way to get rid of them.

164
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:08,759
No need.

165
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:11,720
I'll go meet them myself.

166
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,000
Yue...

167
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,840
Qingqing.

168
00:13:50,519 --> 00:13:51,440
Dad.

169
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,879
Qingqing,

170
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:53,919
listen.

171
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Dad needs to talk to this gentleman.

172
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:57,519
Okay?

173
00:13:57,519 --> 00:13:59,639
Could you go back to your room for now?

174
00:14:00,279 --> 00:14:01,120
Go on.

175
00:14:04,559 --> 00:14:05,320
What's this about?

176
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,399
Hello, Mr. Wu.

177
00:14:06,759 --> 00:14:08,279
The traffic police received a report

178
00:14:08,279 --> 00:14:09,879
stating that Ms. Chen Xue's car

179
00:14:09,879 --> 00:14:11,919
was found on the night of March 20th

180
00:14:11,919 --> 00:14:13,320
parked on Changhong Highway.

181
00:14:13,879 --> 00:14:15,799
But the family already drove it away.

182
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,879
Since this vehicle is critical

183
00:14:17,879 --> 00:14:20,120
physical evidence in this case,

184
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,440
we need to bring the car

185
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,679
back to the station for analysis.

186
00:14:23,159 --> 00:14:24,039
Here are the documents.

187
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:31,960
No problem.

188
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:38,759
Remember, fully cooperate with the police.

189
00:14:38,759 --> 00:14:39,559
Understood?

190
00:14:39,559 --> 00:14:40,039
Understood.

191
00:14:40,039 --> 00:14:40,600
Mm.

192
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,840
We'll take our leave, then.

193
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:52,320
Right.

194
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,600
This way, please.

195
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,600
Come here, come here.

196
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,360
Let Daddy have a look.

197
00:15:15,679 --> 00:15:17,720
What did you draw here?

198
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,120
This is the police lady.

199
00:15:20,679 --> 00:15:22,480
Do you like the police lady?

200
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,240
Yes, I do!

201
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,840
What about you, Daddy?

202
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,720
Me? I like her too. I like her too.

203
00:15:34,039 --> 00:15:34,759
Excuse me, guys.

204
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,559
Does anyone know Su Dahai?

205
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:39,240
What's your business?

206
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:41,720
Oh.

207
00:15:42,919 --> 00:15:43,759
A friend of his.

208
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,519
Su Dahai!

209
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:47,240
Anyone taking this?

210
00:15:48,799 --> 00:15:49,559
What is it?

211
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,039
Three, four, five, six, seven.

212
00:15:53,039 --> 00:15:53,960
You Su Dahai?

213
00:15:56,159 --> 00:15:57,320
Who're you?

214
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:58,840
Are you Su Dahai or not?

215
00:15:59,559 --> 00:16:00,879
Who are you?

216
00:16:00,879 --> 00:16:02,720
I already told the police everything.

217
00:16:03,679 --> 00:16:04,240
Fine.

218
00:16:04,759 --> 00:16:06,200
Come here, let's have a chat.

219
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:08,679
That's pretty much it.

220
00:16:12,039 --> 00:16:12,840
That's all?

221
00:16:13,279 --> 00:16:14,039
Yeah, that's all.

222
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:16,879
Don't you have any enemies or anything?

223
00:16:17,799 --> 00:16:20,600
I'm just a driver. What enemies could I have?

224
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,759
No daily scrapes or fender benders?

225
00:16:24,799 --> 00:16:25,840
Nope.

226
00:16:27,279 --> 00:16:27,720
Oh...

227
00:16:28,039 --> 00:16:30,039
Well, a few days ago, at Qingxi Market,

228
00:16:30,039 --> 00:16:30,759
as I was coming out,

229
00:16:31,759 --> 00:16:33,840
some punk almost smashed my car.

230
00:16:35,519 --> 00:16:36,600
What happened?

231
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,600
I didn't notice a puddle back then,

232
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,080
so I drove right through it.

233
00:16:41,879 --> 00:16:43,879
He seemed to be dragging a big bag,

234
00:16:44,759 --> 00:16:45,960
and water probably splashed on it.

235
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,360
Then he looked like he was gonna attack me,

236
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:50,440
so I didn't dare get out and just sped off.

237
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,960
What did he look like?

238
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,279
I didn't get a good look.

239
00:16:57,720 --> 00:17:00,320
He seemed a bit crazy,

240
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,240
babbling gibberish,

241
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,360
and the way he acted...

242
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,679
he didn't seem quite right.

243
00:17:04,599 --> 00:17:05,079
I...

244
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,160
panicked and just drove off.

245
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:10,319
All right.

246
00:17:10,799 --> 00:17:12,839
Give me the addresses of the eight markets

247
00:17:12,839 --> 00:17:13,680
you've visited.

248
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:20,839
Coming right up!

249
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,759
Excuse me,

250
00:18:13,559 --> 00:18:15,279
Did Qingqing braid this bracelet for you?

251
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:16,359
You want this?

252
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:46,960
Hey, boss.

253
00:18:47,119 --> 00:18:47,440
Yeah?

254
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:48,400
Give me a ribbonfish.

255
00:18:49,799 --> 00:18:51,319
Ribbonfish is saltwater.

256
00:18:51,319 --> 00:18:52,599
I only have freshwater fish here.

257
00:18:54,599 --> 00:18:55,119
Hey.

258
00:18:55,799 --> 00:18:57,000
That guy just now,

259
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:57,920
he seemed pretty interesting.

260
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,640
Didn't say a word, just gestured.

261
00:19:00,279 --> 00:19:01,160
You mean him?

262
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,519
Not only can't he speak,

263
00:19:03,759 --> 00:19:04,839
he's not right in the head, either.

264
00:19:04,839 --> 00:19:06,200
Can't do any heavy work.

265
00:19:06,319 --> 00:19:07,119
What does he do?

266
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:10,400
He used to collect scrap in the market.

267
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:12,119
Then the market manager took pity on him...

268
00:19:12,119 --> 00:19:12,440
All right.

269
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,039
Thanks.

270
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:14,279
Hey! Hey!

271
00:19:14,279 --> 00:19:14,960
Are you buying or not?

272
00:19:18,039 --> 00:19:18,720
Captain Liu,

273
00:19:19,839 --> 00:19:20,799
the technical report is out.

274
00:19:21,839 --> 00:19:24,720
Chen Xue's front-left tire has obvious damage.

275
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,000
It completely matches

276
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,720
the angle iron found at the primary crime scene.

277
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,240
The report also shows

278
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,000
traces of marine microorganisms

279
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,039
and formalin.

280
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,640
Captain Liu, it all lines up.

281
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,039
Here is Su Dahai's statement.

282
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:38,839
We've checked all four food markets.

283
00:19:38,839 --> 00:19:40,039
We can confirm that

284
00:19:40,039 --> 00:19:41,599
the victim's legs were secretly loaded

285
00:19:41,599 --> 00:19:43,000
onto the truck by the killer

286
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,079
while the driver was in the restroom.

287
00:19:44,559 --> 00:19:46,079
Within the overlapping range of

288
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:48,640
Chen Xue's phone and the public restroom,

289
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:49,680
there's a fish market.

290
00:19:55,559 --> 00:19:55,920
Hey.

291
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:57,599
Captain Liu!

292
00:19:58,039 --> 00:19:58,759
Where are you going?

293
00:19:58,759 --> 00:19:59,880
To the fish market.

294
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:00,839
What about us?

295
00:20:00,839 --> 00:20:02,119
Take a break and finish your food.

296
00:20:46,559 --> 00:20:47,519
Chenghao.

297
00:20:59,079 --> 00:21:00,880
This wasn't a one-man job.

298
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:07,960
Bro Hao.

299
00:21:12,039 --> 00:21:12,799
Bro Hao.

300
00:21:43,319 --> 00:21:44,160
Do you recognize her?

301
00:21:44,839 --> 00:21:45,759
You see her, right?

302
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,519
Where did you hide her?

303
00:21:48,279 --> 00:21:49,079
Where is she?

304
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,640
Hey, bro. Bro, bro, bro!

305
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,119
Move!

306
00:21:58,119 --> 00:21:58,519
Bro!

307
00:21:58,519 --> 00:21:59,160
Get out of my way!

308
00:21:59,160 --> 00:21:59,480
Bro!

309
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,720
What is it? What's wrong?

310
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:04,039
Bro.

311
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,799
We haven't gotten anything on Sister Xue yet.

312
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:08,680
Let me try.

313
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,039
Fine.

314
00:22:10,359 --> 00:22:11,079
Let me try.

315
00:22:17,759 --> 00:22:18,759
I'll let you down.

316
00:22:18,759 --> 00:22:19,759
Draw whatever you know.

317
00:22:19,759 --> 00:22:20,640
Understand?

318
00:22:25,519 --> 00:22:26,119
Draw.

319
00:23:01,319 --> 00:23:02,720
What... What is this?

320
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,559
What the hell is this?

321
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,079
Police! We received a tip from the public.

322
00:23:16,079 --> 00:23:17,480
You're ganging up and assaulting people,

323
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,799
which is a criminal offense.

324
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,400
Squat down with your hands on your heads!

325
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,039
Cooperate with the investigation!

326
00:23:25,759 --> 00:23:27,400
Everyone at the scene,

327
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:29,279
bring them to the station for statements.

328
00:23:29,279 --> 00:23:30,319
Yes, sir!

329
00:23:30,319 --> 00:23:31,880
Squat down! Hands behind your head!

330
00:23:41,759 --> 00:23:43,000
What's your name? What year were you born?

331
00:23:43,519 --> 00:23:44,599
Yu Tianze.

332
00:23:44,599 --> 00:23:45,440
Age? Speak up!

333
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:46,680
Twenty-two.

334
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:47,640
What's your name?

335
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:49,079
What about you? What's your name?

336
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:50,279
Lin Tong.

337
00:23:50,279 --> 00:23:51,359
Say it again. Didn't catch that.

338
00:23:51,359 --> 00:23:52,519
Lin Tong. Lin Tong!

339
00:23:53,039 --> 00:23:53,599
Age?

340
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:54,599
How long have you been with Wu Xiang?

341
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,319
How long is "not long"?

342
00:23:56,319 --> 00:23:56,799
What's your name?

343
00:23:56,799 --> 00:23:57,400
What year were you born?

344
00:23:58,240 --> 00:23:58,839
Tianze.

345
00:23:59,000 --> 00:23:59,279
Age?

346
00:23:59,279 --> 00:23:59,960
What's your name?

347
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:00,920
Twenty-six.

348
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:01,839
Go ahead.

349
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:03,000
Why'd you beat him?

350
00:24:04,279 --> 00:24:07,119
Which eye saw me hit anyone, Captain Liao?

351
00:24:09,039 --> 00:24:10,279
Let me rephrase that, then.

352
00:24:10,839 --> 00:24:12,279
Why did you have others beat him?

353
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:14,279
Then you should ask them.

354
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:17,519
Bullying the weak...

355
00:24:17,519 --> 00:24:19,079
Doesn't really seem like your style.

356
00:24:22,559 --> 00:24:23,720
Some people

357
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:25,880
might look weak,

358
00:24:27,759 --> 00:24:29,039
but in truth,

359
00:24:29,039 --> 00:24:31,759
they could easily be lurking right beside us—

360
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:34,400
monsters stripped of humanity.

361
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:42,079
Are you talking about yourself?

362
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,240
Yeah.

363
00:24:44,839 --> 00:24:46,240
I'm a monster, too.

364
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,599
As for his medical bills,

365
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:52,559
I'll pay double.

366
00:24:55,839 --> 00:24:56,440
Come in.

367
00:24:59,000 --> 00:24:59,599
Captain Liao.

368
00:24:59,599 --> 00:24:59,920
Yeah?

369
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,079
The guy over there isn't cooperating either.

370
00:25:01,079 --> 00:25:01,960
Could you come take a look?

371
00:25:02,119 --> 00:25:02,759
All right.

372
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:04,359
Keep going.

373
00:25:04,359 --> 00:25:04,839
Right.

374
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,000
Still not talking, huh?

375
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,599
Still giving us that attitude?

376
00:25:25,799 --> 00:25:27,640
Tonight, our officers were on an operation,

377
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:28,640
and you resisted arrest.

378
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:29,200
Hey,

379
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:31,960
Officer.

380
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:34,160
If I'd resisted arrest,

381
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:35,359
I wouldn't be sitting here right now.

382
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,160
I'm warning you.

383
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:38,599
Watch your attitude.

384
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:40,319
My attitude is great.

385
00:25:40,759 --> 00:25:41,720
Tang Chenghao.

386
00:25:42,559 --> 00:25:43,960
I've seen plenty of guys like you.

387
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:46,000
Do you know where you are?

388
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:46,920
The police station.

389
00:25:47,319 --> 00:25:48,119
As long as you know.

390
00:25:48,599 --> 00:25:49,559
Don't think keeping quiet

391
00:25:49,559 --> 00:25:50,640
means my hands are tied.

392
00:25:50,640 --> 00:25:51,920
48 hours, right?

393
00:25:57,079 --> 00:25:57,640
Captain Liao.

394
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:58,599
You two step outside.

395
00:25:58,599 --> 00:25:59,720
Doesn't matter who you bring in.

396
00:26:14,400 --> 00:26:15,039
Go ahead.

397
00:26:16,839 --> 00:26:17,440
It's fine.

398
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:18,440
Speak.

399
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:21,599
What took you so long?

400
00:26:22,839 --> 00:26:24,559
That guy had Chen Xue's bracelet on him.

401
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,039
Wu Xiang suspects he's the killer.

402
00:26:26,039 --> 00:26:27,000
But I don't think so.

403
00:26:27,759 --> 00:26:29,079
How can you be sure?

404
00:26:29,079 --> 00:26:30,400
Wasn't he brought in?

405
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,440
Didn't you see him?

406
00:26:32,119 --> 00:26:33,359
He's not right in the head,

407
00:26:33,359 --> 00:26:34,720
and he has limited mobility.

408
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:35,839
I just don't think he could possibly be

409
00:26:35,839 --> 00:26:37,200
the one who attacked Chen Xue.

410
00:26:38,319 --> 00:26:40,160
When you tracked him down,

411
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,200
why didn't you report it immediately?

412
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:43,839
If we'd arrived a little later,

413
00:26:43,839 --> 00:26:45,720
he probably would've died at Wu Xiang's hands.

414
00:26:45,720 --> 00:26:47,240
I'd only just tracked him down!

415
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:49,480
Why did Wu Xiang get there faster than us?

416
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:51,359
Where did he get his intel?

417
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,160
Are you suspecting me, Mentor?

418
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:00,000
He showed up right after I found him.

419
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:01,920
He must have other sources of intel.

420
00:27:02,759 --> 00:27:03,960
I'm just worried about you.

421
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:08,079
If Wu Xiang finds the killer,

422
00:27:08,519 --> 00:27:09,759
what do you think will happen?

423
00:27:10,160 --> 00:27:12,000
Don't forget who you are.

424
00:27:12,559 --> 00:27:13,599
Your mission

425
00:27:14,079 --> 00:27:15,279
is to find Snake King.

426
00:27:18,759 --> 00:27:19,960
Look into someone for me.

427
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:22,839
I suspect there's something off about him.

428
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:29,400
Captain Liao.

429
00:27:29,559 --> 00:27:30,000
Yeah?

430
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,079
Captain Liao.

431
00:27:40,519 --> 00:27:41,559
Those three all spilled.

432
00:27:41,559 --> 00:27:43,400
They admitted they were the ones who beat him up.

433
00:27:43,799 --> 00:27:45,400
We're applying for the arrest warrant now.

434
00:27:46,079 --> 00:27:47,400
What about the rest?

435
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:50,000
Let them go.

436
00:27:51,799 --> 00:27:52,279
Okay.

437
00:27:52,279 --> 00:27:52,839
Hey,

438
00:27:53,759 --> 00:27:55,799
what time is the city bureau meeting tomorrow?

439
00:27:55,799 --> 00:27:56,799
Eight in the morning.

440
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:57,920
Got it.

441
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:33,480
Bro,

442
00:28:34,519 --> 00:28:35,799
I was going to look into it

443
00:28:35,799 --> 00:28:36,680
before telling you.

444
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,799
Didn't expect you guys to just show up.

445
00:28:40,359 --> 00:28:41,640
Still, I feel like that guy

446
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:43,640
doesn't seem like the killer.

447
00:28:47,519 --> 00:28:49,759
It's a shame you didn't become a cop.

448
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:57,240
Bro,

449
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,960
you think someone like me still has a shot?

450
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,079
Besides,

451
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:06,599
being a cop isn't nearly as carefree as this.

452
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,279
Damn right.

453
00:29:28,119 --> 00:29:29,039
Ms. Yang,

454
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:32,400
you haven't painted with me in so long.

455
00:29:33,079 --> 00:29:34,519
I missed you so much!

456
00:29:35,799 --> 00:29:37,359
That's why I came back to be with you, right?

457
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:38,279
Mm-hmm.

458
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:40,480
Touch this up a little more. Right here.

459
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:42,400
Yeah, paint right there.

460
00:29:43,079 --> 00:29:43,799
Ms. Yang,

461
00:29:44,079 --> 00:29:45,279
thank you for your time.

462
00:29:45,599 --> 00:29:46,599
This kid

463
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:48,839
has been waiting for you for so long.

464
00:29:50,319 --> 00:29:51,440
When you have time,

465
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:52,680
please spend more time with her.

466
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:57,839
Uncle Tang,

467
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:01,720
stay here and paint with us!

468
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,160
Be good, Qingqing.

469
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:09,039
Let Ms. Yang keep you company for now.

470
00:30:09,880 --> 00:30:11,119
I still have work to do,

471
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:11,960
okay?

472
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,519
Ms. Yang, what's wrong with Uncle Tang?

473
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:28,960
Why is he unhappy?

474
00:30:33,759 --> 00:30:34,599
Qingqing,

475
00:30:34,599 --> 00:30:36,160
Uncle Tang must be tired.

476
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:36,960
Let him get some rest,

477
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:37,480
okay?

478
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:39,480
Let's keep drawing, all right?

479
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:40,279
Come, sit down.

480
00:31:06,440 --> 00:31:07,079
Hey.

481
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:19,839
Why did you come back?

482
00:31:25,279 --> 00:31:26,839
Qingqing called me.

483
00:31:28,599 --> 00:31:29,519
About Sister Xue...

484
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:32,000
I know about it too.

485
00:31:34,839 --> 00:31:36,119
I'll have someone take you back.

486
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:49,039
I like you.

487
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:03,200
No matter who you are.

488
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:03,599
Need a scrub!

489
00:33:04,799 --> 00:33:05,759
Where is everyone?

490
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:07,880
Someone get over here!

491
00:33:28,559 --> 00:33:29,319
The complete set.
